 "rule": "Opponent: the first arm of OPPONENT_ORDER (the brief's order) that was counted, has no voxel with central-difference det <= 0 in the whole volume and at least\none Q1 cell with a witness.  Slab: a slab is the layer of cells between two neighbouring node planes k, k+1 along one axis (three orientations).  Every slab that holds at\nleast one witness cell of the opponent is a candidate; its window is the W x W block of cells centred on the bounding box of the opponent's witness cells in that slab\n(clipped to the volume cropped by 2 voxels), W the first of WINDOWS for which a candidate passes.  Per candidate: a = the opponent's witness cells in the window, b = the\nwitness cells of the pre-repair CertWarp field in the same window, the fraction of the window's nodes (plane k) with fixed > 0.  Chosen: the largest a; among those\n(fraction >= 0.5, b >= 1) the largest b; ties by orientation (axial, coronal, sagittal), then k.  If no candidate with the largest a has b >= 1 at any W, the next a.\nWritten after the 12 witness cells of ants_s had been listed (coordinates, min J, central det at their corners) and before the CertWarp fields were counted.",
